&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripes on the Government Relations &amp;amp; Public Affairs team operate in a fast-paced internal and external environment that requires collaborating with teams across our organization and with outside stakeholders. The culture is thoughtful, transparent, academically rigorous, and kind. In this role, you will have the opportunity to impact the trajectory of Stripe in the US and enhance financial innovation and inclusion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are a team player who wants to represent millions of businesses around the world growing on Stripe, we look forward to hearing from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you will deal with a diverse set of issues that straddle financial services, technology, internet regulation, and economic policy. You will define, shape, and advocate for initiatives that increase the GDP of the Internet. You will maintain deep relationships with Members of Congress, committee staff, key federal regulators, and the Executive Branch — building and executing legislative and regulatory strategies on issues central to Stripe&#39;s mission, including payments modernization, financial regulation, artificial intelligence, and the future of agentic commerce.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role must reside in the DC, Maryland, Virginia area. We are not accepting remote candidates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work as part of our Government Relations &amp;amp; Public Affairs team across the globe to strategically develop, pursue, and execute policy objectives as part of Stripe&#39;s global policy priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and execute federal legislative advocacy — managing Stripe&#39;s engagement with Congress on key legislative priorities including stablecoins, digital assets, open banking, AI governance, and payments regulation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain relationships with Members of Congress, committee and personal staff, and serve as Stripe&#39;s frontline representative on federal legislation affecting the payments and technology industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage federal regulatory agencies — including the Treasury Department, OCC, FDIC, Federal Reserve, CFPB, and others — to educate them about Stripe&#39;s business, advocate for sound policy outcomes, and navigate regulatory proceedings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan, develop, and execute policy initiatives and campaigns that advance Stripe&#39;s policy goals and those of our users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help colleagues across Stripe understand federal legislative and regulatory developments, identify policy opportunities to grow our business, and translate complex policy dynamics into actionable guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe on trade groups, coalitions, and industry bodies engaged on federal policy issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 10+ years of experience in a policymaking, government, or senior advocacy role — ideally a mix of time on Capitol Hill, in a federal regulatory agency, or in a world-class organization as an in-house government relations expert or other business-related role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background working for a Member of Congress, a committee or leadership office, or in a senior policy role at the US Treasury, OCC, FDIC, White House, or comparable federal institution — with a track record of navigating bipartisan legislative environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in financial services regulation and payments policy, with a strong understanding of the legislative and regulatory landscape across banking, money transmission, and digital assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with, and ideally direct experience on, emerging technology policy — including artificial intelligence, agentic commerce, and the regulatory questions that arise at the intersection of AI and financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong relationships with policymakers and staff on both sides of the aisle and a reputation for credibility, reliability, and good judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of managing complex, technical policy issues — capable of managing major initiatives independently, driving coalitions, or project managing a cross-functional team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent judgment — capable of making smart decisions in the face of ambiguity and imperfect information and learning from them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A terrific communicator and writer, adept at working with lawyers, regulators, engineers, business teams, and colleagues to make complex concepts clear and understandable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for Stripe&#39;s mission of helping businesses grow and thrive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, curious team-first mindset with experience thriving in ambiguous, high-growth or startup environments across global offices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathy, humility, and a respect for those who have views that are different from yours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A willingness to work with a diverse group of policy, regulatory, and product professionals who care deeply about Stripe&#39;s policy issues, our users, and each other&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel 25% for meetings and events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Workplace team’s mission is to create and support work environments that are welcoming, comfortable, and intuitive. These spaces are designed to promote collaboration, well-being, and productivity while adhering to the rigorous safety, security, and confidentiality standards required of a financial services company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Workplace Experience team comprises hospitality-focused professionals who partner with the business to shape the daily experiences of Stripes, visitors, and candidates across 20+ global office locations. This geographically dispersed team oversees facilities management, daily operations, and local workplace programs, including events and onsites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a strategic leader and experienced manager with a high EQ who&#39;s enthusiastic about, and has a driving need to deliver, the best possible workplace experience for Stripes. You&#39;ll be a key member of our Experience team and responsible for ensuring that workplace operations, experiences, facilities, and programs run smoothly at our New York office. As a business partner, you have a deep understanding of the needs, experiences, and day-to-day realities of Stripes at your location and build strong relationships not only with site leads but also with cross-functional partners across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires a high level of expertise and operational oversight—from understanding how the building functions top to bottom to governance of contractor team performance and ensuring financial accountability. A key part of the role is anticipating the needs of the business by understanding both the site and the broader context of company growth. You&#39;ll gather and synthesize feedback from multiple sources to ensure the workplace strategy is informed by real insights from the ground. While enterprise workplace strategy is developed centrally, you&#39;re expected to bring informed recommendations based on local business needs and operational insight, and to own successful implementation and adoption at your site.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note this role requires an in office presence of 4 days per week.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee workplace operations at your site(s), providing direction on all workplace services, including building operations, front of house, shipping and receiving, events support, and employee health and safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sound, independent operational decisions by balancing business impact, risk, cost, and employee experience, seeking alignment when decisions create broader organizational impact or precedent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and motivate a team of workplace services professionals, providing direction, coaching, and performance management to drive team excellence and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strong relationships with internal stakeholders, including senior leadership, department heads, and cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a strong rapport with locally assigned Stripes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own operational performance for your site by monitoring service levels and utilization, identifying trends, resolving root causes, and driving continuous improvement across workplace operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively anticipate business needs by understanding both local context and company priorities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop thoughtful, data-informed recommendations that help shape workplace programs and experiences while maintaining alignment with global standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold workplace partners and service providers accountable for performance, ensuring contractual obligations, service levels, and operational standards are consistently achieved while driving continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with our Finance &amp;amp; Strategy partner and IFM partner to develop and oversee the opex budget for all facilities, opex, fixed assets, and events of the NYC office.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the local site leadership team to activate the office by creating engagement, connection, and an inclusive environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft relevant communications and documentation regarding Workplace policies and programs for Stripes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure consistent execution of global workplace programs, standards, and policies at your site,&amp;nbsp; as developed by our Food, Space Planning, and Programs teams, adapting implementation to local operational requirements while maintaining alignment with enterprise objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Workplace team&#39;s goals by taking on ad hoc tasks and projects as they arise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in workplace/hospitality management in a fast-paced environment with a strong customer service orientation and an understanding of operational best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong demonstrated ability in facilities management, vendor, and budget management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strength in building relationships with key internal partners to ensure efficiency and understanding on cross-functional projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a team focused on customer service, hospitality, and operations, with the ability and desire to develop and coach your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to synthesize operational data, stakeholder feedback, and business context into clear recommendations that support sound decision making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Google Suite, Slack and Jira&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear willingness to take a hands-on approach and dive into the details&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to influence cross-functional partners and translate enterprise strategy into effective local execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently, digging into problems to understand the root cause and delivering scalable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to thrive in a fast-paced workplace with rapidly changing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An innovative mindset with the ability to drive exceptional workplace services and operational improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;Workplace Strategy and Operations Manager&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Workplace team is responsible for delivering welcoming, functional, and beautiful environments worldwide. We ensure that Stripe&#39;s real estate portfolio evolves to stay aligned with our mission and the needs of our users, while also ensuring efficient space utilization. As part of the team, you&#39;ll help scale Stripe&#39;s future workspaces, collaborating with stakeholders across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Head of Workplace, the Strategy and Operations Manager will play a key role in driving cross-functional initiatives across our core Workplace pillars (Real Estate Strategy and Transactions, Environments (design and construction), and Experience (workplace services and programs), alongside high-priority &#39;interstitial&#39; projects. You&#39;ll contribute to projects and programs that shape the future of Workplace at Stripe. With the ability to influence from a strategic and administrative perspective, you&#39;ll be instrumental in executing key cross-org initiatives and helping us move from strategy to execution while ensuring operational excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the Head of Workplace in defining SOKRs and ensuring all pillars and cross-functional partners are aligned with the team&#39;s roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional projects that don&#39;t fit neatly into one department. Support M&amp;amp;A integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify bottlenecks in our current workflows and design scalable processes to remove them. Design and lead operating cadences and governance forums to ensure speed, clarity, and accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct deep-dive analyses on business metrics to provide the Workplace Leadership Team with actionable recommendations for growth and efficiency. Drive the Workplace AI and data strategy in partnership with our IT Business Partner. Identify and implement innovative Workplace technologies and systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in strategy and operations, management consulting, corporate real estate strategy, or a data-driven operational role in a fast-growing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong quantitative skills with a track record of using data to drive complex business cases and macro-level decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading large-scale, cross-functional projects from ambiguous conception to rigorous execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly within or alongside Workplace or Real Estate teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great collaboration and people skills, with the ability to build relationships with both leaders and individual contributors across the broader organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High judgment with the ability to balance speed, risk, and organizational health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An inclination to solve problems systematically via infrastructure and automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear willingness to take a hands-on approach and dive into the details&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work independently or with a small team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility with changing requirements in an evolving and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and an ability to build and leverage cross-functional relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to capture complex concepts and communicate them succinctly to key stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an experienced writer to develop data-backed theses and original content pieces around emerging technologies and market trends. In this role, you&#39;ll collaborate closely with contributors across the product marketing, product, engineering, and demand generation teams to produce compelling content that engages and informs our audience. This is a unique opportunity for a collaborative writer who excels at translating complex concepts in fintech, B2B technology, AI, and crypto into accessible insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Own 3–4 focus areas across industries, emerging technologies, and Stripe product pillars, working closely with product marketing to ensure that our content reflects the latest news and product enhancements • Coordinate with the demand generation team to identify opportunities for new editorial series and research agendas&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Pioneer new content formats for Stripe, including short-form content and multimedia projects that grow our audience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Partner with the data science team and third-party agencies to surface relevant insights for existing and potential customers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Ensure consistency and tone in messaging across Stripe channels, including blogs, guides, reports, and social-native content&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Manage a pipeline of content, ensuring clear communication and visibility across the organization&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• A strong writer with 7+ years of experience in journalism, content marketing, or related fields, ideally with a focus on fintech or B2B technology&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• An analytical thinker who can derive original insights from data and market signals&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Skilled at combining various requests and feedback into a unified message&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• A high-quality bar for differentiated content&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Passionate about technology and eager to understand exactly how it works&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Discerning and constructive when giving edits&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Enthusiastic about developing new ways to engage and inform audiences&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Data-driven when making decisions and assessing impact&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Detail-oriented and consistent in your work&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Excited to work in a fast-paced environment where your efforts contribute to a greater goal and align with the company&#39;s mission&lt;/p&gt;
